Description: Stop gala crashing on exit in BackgroundContainer.
 .
 BackgroundContainer's destructor looked up the monitor manager through the
 backend to disconnect its monitors-changed handler. On exit, mutter frees the
 backend before gala's actors are destroyed, so the lookup segfaults in
 meta_backend_get_monitor_manager. The crash makes the gala unit fail, which
 triggers gnome-session-failed and ends the whole session (for example on
 `ep restart gala`).
 .
 The destructor is not needed: Vala connects the handler with
 g_signal_connect_object, which disconnects it when the container is disposed.
--- gala-8.6.1+r3147+pkg134~ubuntu8.1+ep1.orig/src/Background/BackgroundContainer.vala
+++ gala-8.6.1+r3147+pkg134~ubuntu8.1+ep1/src/Background/BackgroundContainer.vala
@@ -39,11 +39,6 @@
         update ();
     }
 
-    ~BackgroundContainer () {
-        unowned var monitor_manager = display.get_context ().get_backend ().get_monitor_manager ();
-        monitor_manager.monitors_changed.disconnect (update);
-    }
-
     private void update () {
         var reference_child = (get_child_at_index (0) as BackgroundManager);
         if (reference_child != null)
